From b3f34db6d7f9697b5e3b8f19ef80a6b15b3e7c8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VecSzn <82099364+VecSzn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:28:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] poly: --conversation-cache-mib auto, sized from the free RAM

setup turned the conversation cache on at a fixed 8192 MiB, whatever
RAM the PC had left beside the model.  Strata's engine sizes it from
the RAM free once the model is loaded, in commit f0010a607f32 ("serve:
the conversation cache is sized from the free RAM when
--conversation-cache-mib is not given (#3493): ..."): 40% of what is
left above the parking floor, at most 8192 MiB, in steps of 256, and
off when that is under 1024.

Take its auto_conversation_cache_mib() and its tests as they are, and
let strata-poly use it for --conversation-cache-mib auto in --serve,
with one log line.  setup writes auto where it wrote 8192 and reads it
back from a saved config.  A number, 0 or no flag mean what they meant
before, so a config setup wrote earlier keeps its 8192.  admit() still
keeps --conversation-cache-min-free-mib free at every park.

On the RTX 4070 laptop (32 GB, Qwen3.6 UD-Q3_K_M), auto gave 2304 to
3072 MiB with 8.6 to 10.5 GB free at start.  With the default 2560 MiB
floor neither auto nor 4096 parks a 2,400-token conversation there:
530 MiB are free once the experts are mapped.  With the floor at 512,
auto (4352 MiB) parked it and brought it back, 2,399 of 2,430 prompt
tokens reused, in 45 ms.  The setup suites pass (694 tests).
